project/ghpages-prebake-modelpool: spoint's ModelPool only engages when the client progressiveReady() probe for <model>.glb.prog/model.progressive.glb returns 200, but that baked asset is produced on-demand by src/static/ProgressiveBake.js which ONLY runs under a live `node server.js`. The static gh-pages host has no server, so on deploy the probe 404s and ModelPool disengages (poolEntities=0) — the map silently renders via the LEGACY EntityLoader instead of the GPU-optimized path. Fix: gh-pages.yml has a build-time 'Bake progressive ModelPool assets' step running bakeProgressive(apps/maps/aim_sillos.glb, dist/apps/maps/aim_sillos.glb.prog) — streaming-gltf's ./bake export, toolchain via its optionalDependencies (CI npm install gets them). MUST run AFTER the optimize-models step (optimize-models.js recurses all subdirs incl .prog and would re-encode/corrupt the meshopt-compressed LOD chunks). LOD paths in LOCAL_progressive extras are relative lods/<f> so the path-patch sed (only *.js/*.html) never touches them. RULE: any new model routed through ModelPool needs its .prog pre-baked into dist for the static deploy.